# Item list pagination

Use `@webonone/ui-kit` **`Pagination`** below **`ItemList`** (or equivalent list body) on any page that shows a pageable collection.

Skill: [.cursor/skills/item-list/SKILL.md](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md) — row layout and menus.

## When required

- API returns `total` + `page` + `pageSize` (server pagination)
- Full list loaded once but UI slices by page (client pagination) when row count can grow

## Layout

```text
FeaturePage
  filters / tabs (optional)
  ItemList → current page rows only
  Pagination → below list (FeaturePage gap-6 applies)
```

## Server pagination

Parent owns `page`, `pageSize`, `total` from API response. On filter/tab change → reset `page` to `1` then fetch.

```typescript
const data = await api.list({ page: nextPage, pageSize, ...filters })
setItems(data.items)
setTotal(data.total)
setPage(data.page)

<Pagination
  totalCount={total}
  currentPage={page}
  pageSize={pageSize}
  onPageChange={(p) => void load(p, pageSize)}
  onPageSizeChange={(size) => { setPageSize(size); setPage(1); void load(1, size) }}
/>
```

Reference: `email/frontend/src/features/history/pages/HistoryPage.tsx`, `queue/pages/QueuePage.tsx`, `dashboard/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`, `templates/pages/TemplateEditorPage.tsx`, `media/.../ScopedFolderBrowser.tsx`.

## Client pagination

Load full array once; slice before passing to list child:

```typescript
const visible = items.slice((page - 1) * pageSize, page * pageSize)
<ItemList>…visible…</ItemList>
<Pagination totalCount={items.length} currentPage={page} pageSize={pageSize} … />
```

Reference: `TemplatesPage.tsx`, `CompaniesPage.tsx`, `SystemThemePage.tsx`.

## Rules

- Import `Pagination` from `@webonone/ui-kit` — no ad-hoc Previous/Next button pairs
- Do not put pagination inside `ItemList`
- `Pagination` does not fetch — parent handles data and preserves filters on page change
- Use `hideWhenSinglePage` default (`true`) unless product needs visible disabled controls

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w <service-root>
```
